`ecg_pipeline/interpret/net1d.py` is vendored verbatim from ECGFounder.
`ecg_pipeline/interpret/tasks.txt` is the ECGFounder diagnostic class list.
The `.pth` checkpoints are downloaded at setup time and are not stored in git.

MIT is permissive: bundling, modification, and commercial use are allowed provided the
copyright notice and permission notice are retained. Retain them.

The pretrained weights expect the input prepared as upstream's `dataset.py` prepares
it, and that file does exactly two things: `nan_to_num` and a global z-score
(`(x - mean) / (std + 1e-8)` over the whole array). It applies no filtering of any kind,
no bandpass, no notch, no baseline removal, no resampling. `waveform.zscore` is that
normalization, and the NaN handling is done more carefully upstream of it (gaps are
trimmed or interpolated per lead rather than zeroed). Nothing else is required.


